#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096611 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096411 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b7d0153-6e0a-5e19-83f1-960811dc5205" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "48334c0c-a49e-5dfb-9f8a-8caa0c22d1f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3625" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=4e^x+ 3x^4 - x^2,$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{ \n                          f'(x)             &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4e^x+3x^{4} - x^2 \\right)\\\n                                             &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4e^x\\right)+\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(3x^{4}\\right) -\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\n\t\t\t\t\t     &= 4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(e^x\\right)+3\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(x^{4}\\right) - 2x \\\t\t\t\n                                             &=  4 e^x+  3 \\cdot 4x^{3} - 2x \\\n                                             &=  4 e^x+  12x^{3} - 2x.\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b7d0153-6e0a-5e19-83f1-960811dc5205" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480109 :question-generator/id #uuid "337ca211-135e-5973-81fe-043f1cf73b4b" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186096611.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b7d0153-6e0a-5e19-83f1-960811dc5205" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8de439e4-f2ba-5ae9-842a-f28efa8a537e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 5e^{x} + 4x^{2} - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093909} {:answer/id #u